# Wysteria Lane homepage shell — browser titles

Routes under `app/(wl-home-v2)/` share `app/(wl-home-v2)/layout.tsx`, which sets:

- **`template: "%s — WysteriaLane.org"`** (em dash, U+2014) for child pages
- **`default: "WysteriaLane.org"`** when no page title is set

## Rules

1. **Root `/` (homepage)**  
   In `app/(wl-home-v2)/page.tsx`, keep **`title: { absolute: "WysteriaLane.org" }`** so the tab is exactly `WysteriaLane.org` (no suffix, no template).

2. **Any new page in this group** (e.g. `app/(wl-home-v2)/about/page.tsx`)  
   Export metadata with a **short page name only**:
   - `export const metadata: Metadata = { title: "About" }`  
   The layout produces **`About — WysteriaLane.org`**.  
   **Do not** append ` — WysteriaLane.org` (or variants) in the page `title` string.

3. **Full custom titles**  
   If a page must bypass the template, use `title: { absolute: "…" }` and document why.

4. **Other app segments** (e.g. `(main)`, archive, auth)  
   They use the root `app/layout.tsx` title template (`WysteriaLane.org` suffix). Do not move archive/auth routes into `(wl-home-v2)` unless the product intent is to rebrand those tabs to `— WysteriaLane.org`.

## Checklist

- [ ] New v2-era route lives under `app/(wl-home-v2)/…`
- [ ] Homepage still uses `title.absolute: "WysteriaLane.org"`
- [ ] Child pages use plain `title: "Name"` only (suffix comes from the group layout)
